invariant: INV-4
file: srv.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: ch_srv_check draws four bytes before it checks the identities.
  srv.c is not one of the six files that hold the ten admitted calls, so
  inv-4-randomness-files refuses it. This call passed while
  srv_config_ok's header was split across #if and #else, because Semgrep
  skipped the whole file; a split header now fails tools/semgrep-parse.py
  instead.

--- old
int ch_srv_check(const ch_cfg *cfg) {
    uint8_t live = srv_identity_live(cfg);
--- new
int ch_srv_check(const ch_cfg *cfg) {
    uint8_t probe[4];
    ch_rand_bytes(probe, sizeof probe);
    uint8_t live = srv_identity_live(cfg);
